<title>FRANCE: BA, Groupe Rivaud in Air Liberte bid.</title>
<headline>BA, Groupe Rivaud in Air Liberte bid.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Airways Plc French TAT unit and the Rivaud Group, headed by Vincent Bollore, have joined forces to make a bid to continue the business of ailing Air Liberte, the airlines' administrator said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Rivaud was part of the consortium headed by Jacques Maillout, chairman of Nouvelles Frontieres.</p>
<p>&quot;It's a bid to continue the company. British Airways will have 70 percent, Rivaud 30 percent. It's a bid which satisfies my conditions, assures the jobs and is also good for the creditors,&quot; Maitre Baronnie said by telephone.</p>
</text>
